# Platforms

Platform guides own compilation-target boundaries and filesystem locations shared across the framework. Client pages own transport construction; server pages own protocol-specific runtime dependencies.

## Choose a task

| Task | Guide |
|---|---|
| select facade features, native or Wasm targets, backends, and registration behavior | <GuideRef slug="framework/platforms/features-and-targets">Features and targets</GuideRef> |
| resolve typed config, data, cache, state, runtime, and log directories | <GuideRef slug="framework/platforms/application-directories">Application directories</GuideRef> |

## Shared prerequisites

Identify the application host and deployment targets first. For a browser build, continue into <GuideRef slug="clients/browser">browser clients</GuideRef> after separating native-only dependencies.
